WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.055
Step seven switches to a second
shell, a POSIX shell at the root of

2
00:00:04.055 --> 00:00:08.362
your copy of the repository, and
moves into the drift pipeline folder.

3
00:00:08.362 --> 00:00:12.888
The runs it packages are the repository's
copies of the two days you just made.

4
00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:17.362
Package day one, then day two,
chained to day one's manifest.

5
00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:19.600
Each prints one line of JSON.

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.850
The second says nineteen findings are new,
eighty are open, and one is resolved.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.238
Step eight verifies the
second package three ways.

8
00:00:28.238 --> 00:00:31.725
The packager's own verify
reports twenty-one files.

9
00:00:31.725 --> 00:00:35.539
The standard checksum tool,
run against the checksum file,

10
00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:37.525
prints nothing and exits zero.

11
00:00:37.525 --> 00:00:41.864
And a search of the summary for the
fictional tenant's domain counts zero:

12
00:00:41.864 --> 00:00:44.250
no user principal name is in the summary.

13
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:48.460
That's the check an ISSO can run
with nothing but standard tools.
